# Three services build from the repository root, so without this the whole tree
# is sent to the Docker daemon on every build. A local `.venv` alone is around
# 96 MB of the repository's 109 MB, and Docker does not read `.gitignore`.
#
# Everything a build needs is copied explicitly by the Dockerfile, so this list
# only has to be good enough to keep the context small -- an entry too many
# costs nothing, an entry missing costs build time.

.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore

.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache

# setuptools leaves these in packages/ after a local install. Copying them in
# would have the build inside the image read another machine's metadata.
**/build
**/*.egg-info

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Images and local reference material. Evidence reaches the platform through the
# upload workflow and the blob container, never through an image.
evidence_images
demo-evidence
docs

# Only this one. The Common Event Model's pyproject.toml declares its README, so
# a `**/README.md` rule here would make `pip install ./packages/...` fail inside
# the image on a file that is not even shipped.
/README.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
infra
scripts

# Tests run in CI before the image is built, and the services do not need them
# at runtime.
**/tests
**/requirements-dev.txt
**/pytest.ini
